Parse a constant `_time` column once instead of once per row.

Blocks handed to VL by an external storage backend can carry a `_time` column
whose values are all the same string: the lakehouse cold tier answers
count-class queries from manifest metadata, where every row of a file shares
one timestamp. mustInitFromDataBlock routes `_time` through tryParseTimestamps,
which parsed every value, making a metadata-only answer cost O(rows) RFC3339
parsing even though the column holds a single distinct value.

Detect the constant column with VL's own areConstValues and parse once. No
semantic change: a constant column yields the same timestamps either way, and
a value that fails to parse still falls back to the regular column path.

